  partName: Cylinder Head Bolt (5)
  description: The Cylinder Head Bolt (5) is a tiny, complex-shaped fastener positioned
    at the top-center-center of the engine, fabricated from Material.001. As one
    of the multiple bolts securing the cylinder head, it helps to distribute the
    clamping force evenly, ensuring a reliable seal and preventing potential engine
    damage. Interestingly, the bolt's complex shape allows it to resist loosening
    due to vibration, maintaining a consistent, high-performance engine operation.
